course: dictionary
lesson: 6844
title: One word, many meanings: output
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Output is a word that changes its meaning depending on where you find it. You can say the output of a factory is how much it makes, or that a computer's output is what it gives out, like words on a screen. Look at the words around it to find the right meaning. «Every computer job has three parts: input, processing and output» tells you output is the part that comes out of a computer.
explain: Input and output are opposites. Input is what goes in, and output is what comes out. In maths, a function machine works this way: the input goes in, the rule is followed, and the output comes out. If the rule is × 3 and the input is 4, the output is 12.
explain: Output can also be a verb. To output something means to produce it or give it out. A computer outputs sound through its speakers, so the word works as an action as well as a thing.
fact: Output means what comes out, like a printout, a picture or sound from a computer.
fact: «A speaker is an output device and a microphone is an input device.»
fact: In maths, a function machine takes an input, follows a rule and gives an output.
fact: In science and economics, output can mean how much is made, as in «power output» or «factory output».
fact: «Haptic feedback is small motors vibrating to give a feeling of touch; it is output, not the controller feeling anything.»
exercise: In «Every computer job has three parts: input, processing and output», what is the output? | The instructions the computer follows | *What comes out, like pictures or sound | What goes in, like key presses or clicks | The machine itself
exercise: A function machine has the rule × 3. If the input is 4, what is the output? | *12 | 4 | 43 | 7
exercise: «A speaker is an output device and a microphone is an input device.» Which of these is an output device? | A mouse | *A speaker | A keyboard | A microphone
test: In science and economics, «power output» means what? | The cost of the machine | A warning light | The power that goes into a machine | *The amount of power that is produced
test: As a verb, to output something means what? | To take something in | To delete a file | *To produce or give something out | To ask a question
exam: In «A computer is a machine that takes information in, follows a list of instructions to change it, and gives a result out», which word names the result that comes out? | instructions | *output | processing | input
